{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a sorted set kept in a skip list (Pugh, 1990): sorted linked lists stacked in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"levels, each level a random sample of the one below, searched from the top level down. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element’s tower gains a level with probability 1\/4, so lookup, insertion and removal take","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") expected time with no rebalancing. Its elements are a random-access collection in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending order, indexed by rank, with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowerBound(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"upperBound(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(in:)"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the API matches the sorted sets of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinarySearchTrees"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SkipLists","","var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","numbers.contains(2)     \/\/ false","numbers.lowerBound(5)   \/\/ 3, the index of 5"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation; a seeded one makes every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list reproducible. The list’s levels are a directed acyclic graph, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes to Grafluent’s algorithms and drawings as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(import Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphProtocols"},{"type":"text","text":" module beside this one): a vertex for each element on each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level of its tower, an edge along each level and an edge down each tower."}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SkipLists"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"SkipLists","externalID":"SkipLists"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sorted sets","anchor":"Sorted-sets","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/skiplists"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList/layersView-swift.property":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The list’s levels as a directed graph: a vertex for each element on each level of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tower, an edge from each to the next element on the same level, and an edge from each down"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the same element on the level below. The head is not a vertex."}],"role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text"